
	This install applies to "Stardust" © 1993 Bloodhouse


	This install requires WHDLoad and RawDIC to be in the path.
	Both can be found in the WHDLoad package.
	To install from a different drive than DF0: select Expert as
	installation mode.

	You need 1.0 MB ChipMem and 0.5 MB OtherMem.
	You can quit the game by pressing F10 (key can be changed with
	Tooltype "QuitKey=")


	Features:
	- full load from HD
	- copy protection removed
	- access faults fixed
	- blitter waits inserted
	- load/save highscore + password
	- skip intro option (set CUSTOM1=1 tooltype) 
	- nice NI/MWB icons included,

	Thanx to:
	- Chris Vella for original disk images.

	version 1.0 (??-Mar-2000) done by Mr Larmer
	- first public release

	version 1.1 (27-Mar-2000) done by Mr Larmer
	- all levels work

	version 1.2 (13-Dec-2000) done by Bored Seal:
	- level password is saved
	- highscore is saved to separated file now.
	- highscores are saved even for unregistered users now
	- access faults fixed
	- disk access removed

	version 1.3 (09-Jan-2001) done by Bored Seal
	- intro sound works again (my bug, sorry)
	- 6x blitter waits in intro and asteroid part added
	- CACR operation removed
	- skip intro option added (set custom1=1 for faster boot)

	version 1.4 (26-Jun-2006) done by Wepl
	- fixed to be compatible with WHDload v16.6 (resload_Control)
	- uses 'data' sub directory
	- new install script
	- source included
	- an os3.5 icon, manual and hints added

	version 1.5 (13-Nov-2017) done by StingRay
	- 68000 quitkey support
	- support for fire button 2 added (to access weapon menu)
	- Bplcon0 color bit fixes
	- blitter wait added
	- WHDLoad v17+ features used (config)

	version 1.6 (26-Dec-2022) done by StingRay
	- crash when quitting after tunnel sequence fixed (issue #5548)
	- graphics problems when starting level fixed (introduced in V1.5)
	
	version 1.6, #2 (26-Dec-2022) done by StingRay
	- old V1.5 slave was still in the archive, now the correct slave
	  is included (thanks Retroplay)

	version 1.6, #3 (26-Dec-2022) done by StingRay
	- all good things come in threes, data directory path fixed
	  (thanks to Retroplay again)
	  
	  version 1.7 (24.08.2026) done by Arise from Decay
	  - trainer added
	  - no highscores will be saved when any trainer or levelselect is used
	
           for full WHDLoad package and other installs refer to:
